  "description": "OKUMUF crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C108 H120 Ce6 O60,8(C1 H3 N1 O2),2(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Ce1 (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce2 (Ce) has 9 O neighbors; Ce3 (Ce) has 9 O neighbors; Ce1A (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce2A (Ce) has 9 O neighbors; Ce3A (Ce) has 9 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 12 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.753-3.828 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 114.37-119.73°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Ce6O4(OH)4(H2O)4(dmb)12]·8MeNO2·2H2O (dmb = 2,6-dimethoxybenzoate). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 4 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
